WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.069
-Have a seat.
We have lots to talk about.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.337
-The last time I was here,
we were in the other studio,

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.475
and this is just so amazing
to see everyone.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.110
-It's the greatest, yeah.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.878
Thanks so much for being here.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.680
-Oh, my God. I love you.
-I love you so much.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.050
What do we have to get into?
We have so much to get into.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.351
I'm going to start
with Halloween

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.186
because I think I'm going to
see you this weekend.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.054
-Yeah.
-The kids are gonna hook up.

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.489
-The producers were like,
you know,

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.224
"What are you gonna be doing
for Halloween?"

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:27.660
I was like, "Ironically,
I'll be with Jimmy."

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.229
-We're actually hanging out.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.764
-Are they carving pumpkins?
-We've been carving pumpkins.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.834
We got hu-- This guy, weirdly,

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.536
got us a pumpkin
at this pumpkin patch,

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.639
and we couldn't carry it.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.608
-Wait. Sorry.
You were at a pumpkin patch.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.178
-Yes!
-We're not surprised about that.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.112
But then a guy --
-I love the patch!

00:00:47.112 --> 00:00:49.115
-A guy got you a pumpkin?

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.650
-Weirdly, I had
this whole life lesson

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.752
with Olive about letting it go.

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:54.987
We couldn't carry it.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.089
You've got to, like,
make your peace with it.

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:58.858
And she really did.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.259
And then we got
to the checkout stand,

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:03.029
and this guy
wheelbarrowed it up,

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.832
and we both started crying.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.836
-Because you already said
goodbye to that pumpkin.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.739
-And she had, like,
learned to love and let go.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.874
And then I started crying,
and then we were like,

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.476
"It's a Halloween miracle!"

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.945
-Miracle! Oh, my God.
A Halloween miracle. Please.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:24.283
-And then he had this beautiful,
like, Jesus around his neck.

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.786
And I started having,
like, a religious moment.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.020
-Oh, my God.
-I did.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.656
-You thought it was Jesus
bringing you a pumpkin?

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.926
-Yes! And I was like,
"Thank you so much."

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.828
Then here is the weirdest thing.
I was like -- First of all --

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.431
Then also as a parent,
I started spiraling.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.566
I wanted to be like, "I don't
know. This isn't the lesson.

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.568
This isn't the lesson!"

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.303
The lesson was let it go!

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:45.772
Not you get it!

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.507
-You get anything you want.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.475
-So I'm, like, paralyzed
as a parent,

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:52.312
like, not knowing how to handle
this situation.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:55.381
I want to make it okay for him.
I want her to learn her lesson.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.451
I -- And then also I'm like,
"I got to pay you back.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.954
I want to say thank you."
He's like, "No."

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.088
And I'm like,
"Can I get your phone number

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:05.692
just so I can, you know,
pay you back and say..."

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:08.161
"No." He wanted nothing.
-Wow.

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.964
And then he just walked on water
away from you guys.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.565
-Yes! 100%!

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.568
-That was really --
It was him or Peter Sellers.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.203
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.239
-Chauncey Gardiner!
-Chauncey Gardiner.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.307
I knew you'd like that one.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.509
-The Halloween miracle.
-The Halloween miracle.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.044
So you got a giant pumpkin.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.912
-Yes!
-I wanna see this.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:30.549
-And then we carved it,
and we saved all the seeds,

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.184
and we had this whole ceremony.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:35.721
And I said, you know,
we can't send him a picture,

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:38.091
and he didn't want anything
in return,

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:40.225
because, you know,
he's a saint.

00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:41.594
Literally.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.396
-He's not real, yeah.
Of course.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.364
-If he ever hears this story,

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:47.567
like, you really made me
and my daughter cry.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.968
And the pumpkin's beautiful.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.836
And it did make us
believe in miracles.

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:52.104
-Yeah. Why not?

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:53.473
"The Pumpkin Miracle."
I love that.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:56.275
Look for it next holiday season.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.744
-Coming to Hallmark Channel.
-Coming to Hallmark.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.646
I want to talk
about your cookbook.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:03.248
I know how hard you worked
on this thing.

00:03:03.248 --> 00:03:05.117
I know how much you love
cookbooks.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.719
You have a cookbook collection.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.987
We both have read cookbooks
together.

00:03:08.987 --> 00:03:10.889
-You and I are big --
-I'm obsessed with cookbooks.

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:12.091
-Ever since -- I mean,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.327
we've known each other
for a very long time.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.530
And you have always felt like

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.665
chefs are rock stars,
and I feel the same way.

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:22.701
Like, I'm very intimidated,
blown away by, and, like,

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.704
[ Gasps ]
"That chef just walked in!"

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:28.908
-Yeah. I love it. I think
they're almost like athletes.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.409
-Yes!
-You come here and you go like,

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.645
"Oh, I can throw a football."
And you go, "Not really.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.513
Drew Brees can throw
a football."

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.282
And then you've got a chef
who comes on.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.717
You go like,
"I know how to make pasta."

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.619
You go, "No, you don't have to
make --" It's just amazing.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.854
-Who are your heroes?
And a lot of mine --

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:45.091
And I also think the food
industry is so nurturing,

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.194
and they take care of each other
and they take care of us

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:50.663
and there are memories to be
made and food is a privilege.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.298
So it's just been something

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.533
that's been at the forefront
of my universe.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:04:00.306
But I didn't want to
pretend to be the,

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:01.974
you know, me and my kitchen.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:04.544
I'm so not that guy.
-No.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:08.414
-So I put 300 of
my personal photographs.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.516
I wrote the whole thing
with Pilar.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.952
It's very personal.
-Yeah.

00:04:13.952 --> 00:04:15.688
-And I took that picture.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.958
And I was like, "How can I make
a book that isn't going to

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.727
give me imposter syndrome
into a world

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:24.363
I'm so humble
and freaked out about?"

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:29.736
And so it's very personal, which
made it take so much more work.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.637
-Yeah, because you were like,
"I'm not just going to throw

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:34.040
something out there just to
have a cookbook out there."

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.608
-Writing hundreds of pages.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:38.110
There is -- By the way,
there's me at the patch.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.847
-Wait. This can't be --
This is not this recent.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.481
-That's a different pumpkin.

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.417
-What?!
-Yeah.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.752
That's the year before.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.486
-Did a man give this to you?

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:48.821
-No. And guess what.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.523
That pumpkin did not come home
with me.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.325
He stayed there in the patch.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:55.027
-So you just gave it love
and then let it be.

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:56.128
-Yeah.
-That's another --

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:57.730
-'Cause who is carrying that?

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.065
There's no one to help you.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.300
It's you and a wheelbarrow.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.235
Unless the saint comes along.

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:05.705
-Yeah, yeah,
a miracle comes along.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:08.741
-And I love food,
and I love cooking, and I --

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.310
-I did make this one,
by the way, the pasta.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.812
The creamy, like, lemon
and the peas.

00:05:13.812 --> 00:05:16.248
-It's the best. It's a
[Italian accent] mascarpone.

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:17.983
[ Normal voice ]
This is my favorite cheese

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:19.418
to cook pasta with,
and I love adding the --

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.287
-And they're also the band
tonight.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.822
Mascarpone is here.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.956
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:26.792
-By the way, talk about,
like, I got shy.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.894
I saw them in the hallway
and I was like, "Oh, wow.

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:30.196
They look really cool."

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:31.230
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.698
-They were saying
the same about you.

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:34.232
-Oh, no.

00:05:34.232 --> 00:05:36.268
-I think you're doing
such a great job on the show.

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:37.503
You know I watch.

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.372
I'm a religious -- I watch
your show every morning.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.274
-I don't know what I would
have done without you

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:44.110
because we were launching
in a pandemic.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.645
You were such
a brother and guider.

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:47.813
-I go, "What other person
would launch a show

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.615
during a pandemic
except for you?"

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:50.983
But you did it.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.119
-And we did this book
in a pandemic.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:58.724
And I think this is just
a great time to not pretend,

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:03.629
but peel back the layers
and be more ourselves than ever

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:07.533
and celebrate our little,
beautiful, weird individuality

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:11.604
and cheer each other on and
share our lives and experiences.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:13.372
I was so optimistic
in the pandemic

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:16.441
when people were cooking
the same things together online

00:06:16.441 --> 00:06:18.678
to have some form of community.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:21.447
That gave me a sign, like,
maybe I should proceed

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:27.552
with this project and create
an intimacy and not a veneer.

00:06:27.552 --> 00:06:29.889
-Yeah. It is very you.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:31.223
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:33.425
"Rebel Homemaker."

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:35.294
"Rebel Homemaker"
is the name of the book.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.663
November 2nd it is out.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:40.332
And always watch
"The Drew Barrymore Show"

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.068
on every single morning.

